A Zip64 uncompressed-size in the range [2^63, 2^64) casts to a negative int64 in zip.File.FileInfo().Size(), and ReadZipReader does signed arithmetic on that value, so the total-decompression guard is bypassed and the negative size reaches make([]byte, 0, size) in readFile. A 159-byte crafted file panics OpenFile and OpenReader with runtime error: makeslice: cap out of range.

